From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:22:16 +0900
Subject: KWin moto16: a minimum size above the maximum no longer disconnects
 the client

WeChat 4.1 (static Qt 6) sizes its main window's maximum from Qt's primary
screen, the first wl_output KWin announces (the 360 px wide phone), while
its minimum width is larger; the invalid_size protocol error killed it right
after logging in, also when the window was on the TV. KWin now logs the
conflict and drops the conflicting maximum instead. Verified with a
wayland-client probe committing min 700x400 / max 360x800.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [deviates from xdg-shell: a maximum below the minimum is a protocol
 error (xdg-shell.xml, set_max_size/set_min_size); works around WeChat 4.1, whose static Qt 6 takes
 the maximum from the first wl_output; the fix belongs in the client]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:testXdgShellWindow::testMinimumAboveMaximum; probe:plasma/diagnostics/wayland-probes/minmax-probe.c
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/42
Origin: vendor, commit:f47ee505
